{
	// The CLI is JavaScript with JSDoc types, exactly as upstream's is — the
	// published surface is `.mjs` plus hand-written `.d.ts` declarations, so
	// there is no emit step and no build artifact. `checkJs` is what makes the
	// JSDoc load-bearing: it is the only thing type-checking the manifest
	// builder, the JSON envelopes, and every `@param` in `api/`.
	//
	// `moduleResolution: bundler` mirrors upstream's root tsconfig, and is not
	// incidental: the JSDoc type references are extensionless
	// (`import('./manifest').CLIManifest`) because they point at a sibling
	// `.d.ts` with no runtime file behind it. Under `nodenext` every one of them
	// is an error demanding a `.mjs` extension that would not resolve. Runtime
	// imports keep their real `.mjs` extensions regardless, so Node is unaffected
	// — nothing here is ever emitted or bundled.
	//
	// Upstream splits this across four tsconfigs (`tsconfig.strict.json`,
	// `tsconfig.json-api.json`, `tsconfig.authoring-contract.json`,
	// `tsconfig.template-docs.json`) because it type-checks different subsets at
	// different strictness. This port starts strict everywhere and has no legacy
	// subset to carve out, so one config covers it.
	"compilerOptions": {
		"target": "es2023",
		"lib": ["es2023"],
		"module": "esnext",
		"moduleResolution": "bundler",
		"types": ["node"],

		"allowJs": true,
		"checkJs": true,
		"noEmit": true,

		"strict": true,
		"skipLibCheck": true,
		"esModuleInterop": true,
		"forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
		"resolveJsonModule": true
	},
	// `authoring/**` is not optional here, and not merely for coverage. Three
	// parsers carry a compile-time drift-lock — a JSDoc `@typedef` of
	// `Expect<Equal<…>>` asserting the sealed zod schema still infers exactly the
	// public type. Those only fire under `checkJs`, so leaving the directory out
	// of `include` compiles them as dead comments and the schema-to-type lock
	// silently does nothing. Upstream isolates this in a fourth tsconfig
	// (`tsconfig.authoring-contract.json`); this config is already strict
	// everywhere, so one glob covers it.
	"include": [
		"api/**/*",
		"authoring/**/*",
		"clients/**/*",
		"foundation/**/*",
		"bin/**/*",
		"scripts/**/*"
	],
	// Suites and the in-process harness are excluded, as upstream's
	// `tsconfig.strict.json` excludes `**/*.test.mjs`. They monkeypatch
	// `process.exit`/`console`/`stdout` and read Commander internals off untyped
	// objects; type-checking them would mean either casts on nearly every line or
	// a second, looser config. eslint still covers them.
	//
	// `**/*.d.mts` is excluded for a reason that is nearly invisible and that
	// silently disarmed every drift-lock in `authoring/` the day they landed.
	// TypeScript groups extensions as `[.mts, .d.mts, .mjs]` and, for a
	// *wildcard-matched* path, keeps only the highest-priority extension sharing
	// a basename. So `authoring/config/parse.d.mts` **evicts**
	// `authoring/config/parse.mjs` from the program entirely — the file is not
	// checked, its `Expect<Equal<…>>` typedef is a dead comment, and mutating the
	// schema it guards produces no error at all. Adding `authoring/**` to
	// `include` (see above) was necessary and not sufficient; `--listFiles`
	// showed the three `.d.mts` present and not one `parse.mjs`.
	//
	// Excluding the declaration files restores all of them. They cannot simply be
	// deleted — `authoring/index.d.ts` re-exports value bindings from `./*.mjs`
	// and a downstream build without `allowJs` needs them to resolve — and
	// `exclude` is preferred over upstream's include-shape
	// (`authoring/**/*.mjs` + `authoring/**/*.ts`, which never matches `.d.mts`)
	// because it also covers `authoring/doctypes/*/parse.d.mts` and any future
	// `api/**/*.d.mts` without a second edit.
	//
	// Verified by mutation, not by reading: with this line, changing
	// `integrations: z.array(z.string())` to `z.array(z.number())` fails
	// `authoring/config/parse.mjs` with TS2344 "Type 'false' does not satisfy the
	// constraint 'true'". Without it, the same mutation typechecks clean.
	"exclude": ["node_modules", "**/*.test.mjs", "**/*.d.mts", "test-utils"]
}
